      "content": "The problem is the IT guys are saying Lexis-Lite is basically the same thing, just faster. They're claiming the nuance you provide isn't really necessary for the standard casework we do here. We're trying to move toward more automation and less 'heavy lifting' on the reasoning side to keep costs down. Is there anything we actually need to worry about with the switch?",
